.TH "ALLOYCTL" "1" "Aug 15, 2026" "0.2.1" "alloyctl"
.SH NAME
alloyctl \- Linux CLI to control and configure SteelSeries devices
.SH LINUX CLI TO CONTROL AND CONFIGURE STEELSERIES DEVICES
.SS SYNOPSIS
.sp
\fBalloyctl\fP [\fIOPTIONS\fP]
.SS DESCRIPTION
.sp
\fBalloyctl\fP is a lightweight, dependency\-free configuration tool and full\-screen
terminal user interface for SteelSeries mice and keyboards on Linux.
.sp
When invoked without device\-modifying arguments, \fBalloyctl\fP discovers connected
devices and launches an interactive ncurses\-based dashboard allowing live adjustments
of sensor resolution (CPI/DPI), USB polling rates, per\-zone RGB illumination,
button remapping, Windows/Meta key lock, and onboard flash persistence.
.sp
When invoked with command\-line flags, \fBalloyctl\fP performs the requested
configuration changes non\-interactively, applies them to the target hardware,
updates the local baseline state, and exits immediately.
.SS OPTIONS
.SS General Options
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B  \-h\fP,\fB  \-\-help
Display a summary of available command\-line options, descriptions, and examples,
then exit.
.TP
.B  \-v\fP,\fB  \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.B  \-l\fP,\fB  \-\-list
List all supported SteelSeries device models, device types (mouse or keyboard),
and their corresponding USB Vendor and Product IDs (VID:PID).
.TP
.BI \-d\fP,\fB  \-\-device \ <VID:PID>
Target a specific connected device identified by hexadecimal Vendor ID and
Product ID (for example, \fB1038:1824\fP). If omitted, \fBalloyctl\fP auto\-selects
the connected device or presents an interactive chooser if multiple devices are attached.
.TP
.B  \-\-dump\-udev
Generate standard udev rules granting unprivileged read/write access to
supported \fB/dev/hidraw*\fP nodes for all registered drivers, then exit.
.UNINDENT
.SS Common Configuration Options
.sp
These options apply to both mouse and keyboard devices.
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.BI \-\-brightness \ <0\-100>
Set global LED illumination brightness percentage (0 to 100).
.TP
.BI \-\-polling \ <hz>
Set the USB report rate in Hertz (for example, 125, 250, 500, or 1000 Hz).
.TP
.BI \-\-color \ <[zone:]hex>
Set illumination color using a 6\-character hex code (\fBRRGGBB\fP, optionally
prefixed with \fB#\fP) or CSS 3\-character shorthand (\fBRGB\fP). An optional zero\-based
zone index may prefix the hex code to target a specific LED zone (for example,
\fB0:FF0000\fP for zone 0 red, or \fB00FF88\fP for all zones).
.TP
.BI \-\-fx \ <[zone:]mode>
Set lighting effect mode. Supported values include \fBsteady\fP / \fBstatic\fP (mode 0),
\fBbreath\fP / \fBbreathing\fP (mode 1), or a driver\-defined numeric mode ID. An optional
zero\-based zone index may prefix the mode (for example, \fB1:breath\fP).
.TP
.B  \-\-save
Commit the live configuration settings to the device\(aqs onboard flash memory so
they persist across power cycles and system reboots.
.UNINDENT
.SS Mouse Configuration Options
.sp
These options apply exclusively to mouse devices. Passing them when targeting a keyboard
will result in an error.
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.BI \-\-dpi \ <cpi>\fR,\fB \ \-\-cpi \ <cpi>
Set the primary sensor CPI (counts per inch) resolution. The value is automatically
clamped to the sensor\(aqs supported minimum, maximum, and step size.
.TP
.BI \-\-accel \ <0\-100>
Configure host\-side pointer acceleration curve intensity (0 to 100).
.TP
.BI \-\-decel \ <0\-100>
Configure host\-side pointer deceleration curve intensity (0 to 100).
.TP
.BI \-\-snap \ <0\-45>
Set host\-side angle snapping threshold in degrees (0 to disable).
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-high\-efficiency [on|off]
Toggle the wireless power\-saving high\-efficiency mode (supported wireless devices only).
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.BI \-\-accel\-daemon \ <VID:PID>
Launch the host\-side evdev pointer transform daemon in the background for the specified
device.
.TP
.BI \-\-accel\-stop \ <VID:PID>
Terminate any running host\-side pointer transform daemon for the specified device.
.UNINDENT
.SS Keyboard Configuration Options
.sp
These options apply exclusively to keyboard devices. Passing them when targeting a mouse
will result in an error.
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-meta\-lock [on|off], \-\-win\-lock [on|off]
Enable or disable the Windows / Meta key lock. When enabled (\fBon\fP or \fB1\fP),
accidental Windows key presses during gaming are suppressed in hardware.
.UNINDENT
.SS INTERACTIVE TUI MODE
.sp
Running \fBalloyctl\fP with no configuration arguments launches the full\-screen terminal interface.
.SS Keybindings
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBTab / Shift\-Tab\fP: Navigate between panes.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBUp / Down / j / k\fP: Navigate settings, presets, and color palettes within the active pane.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSpace / Enter\fP: Toggle checkboxes, activate presets, or select buttons.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBS\fP: Save live configuration to device onboard flash.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBQ / Ctrl\-C\fP: Quit \fBalloyctl\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.SS CONFIGURATION FILES
.sp
State files are stored in INI format under:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/alloyctl/<vendor>_<product>.conf\fP
(defaults to \fB~/.config/alloyctl/<vendor>_<product>.conf\fP)
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
These files preserve user settings across sessions and configure parameters such as
active CPI levels, per\-zone illumination colors, polling rates, and button bindings.
.SS EXIT STATUS
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B 0
Success. Requested command, configuration change, or TUI session completed cleanly.
.TP
.B 1
Error. Invalid command\-line argument, invalid option value, unsupported hardware
capability, device\-type mismatch, or missing permission to access \fB/dev/hidraw*\fP / \fB/dev/uinput\fP\&.
.TP
.B 130
Interactive device selection menu was cancelled by user (SIGINT / Esc / Q).
.UNINDENT
.SS EXAMPLES
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B Launch interactive TUI:
$ alloyctl
.TP
.B Set DPI to 1600 and polling rate to 1000 Hz on Rival 3:
$ alloyctl \-\-device 1038:1824 \-\-dpi 1600 \-\-polling 1000 \-\-save
.TP
.B Set illumination brightness to 50% and enable Windows key lock on keyboard:
$ alloyctl \-\-brightness 50 \-\-meta\-lock on
.TP
.B Set LED zone 0 to green (\fB#00FF00\fP) with static effect:
$ alloyctl \-\-color 0:00FF00 \-\-fx 0:steady
.TP
.B Generate udev rules for unprivileged device access:
$ alloyctl \-\-dump\-udev | sudo tee /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/71\-alloyctl\-hidraw.rules
$ sudo udevadm control \-\-reload && sudo udevadm trigger
.UNINDENT
.SS SEE ALSO
.sp
